Subject: [PATCH] speech: persona voices without a host engine

speechSynthesis.getVoices() lists the profile's voices even when the host
has no speech engine, as on a Linux server without speech-dispatcher or
while the engine is still starting. A listed voice is spoken by a host
voice of its own kind, local or network, when there is one. Otherwise,
as for a network voice in a build without API keys, speak() fires start,
then end after about fifteen characters a second at the utterance's
rate, with no audio; pause, resume and cancel act on that clock and send
the events a real voice of that kind sends. Before this a Windows persona
on a Linux server listed no voices, which no Windows machine does.

